    <node id="Military Special Video Command Control System">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">A military-specific video command and control system based on network communication. It is an important component of the military command information system, accompanying joint operations in the information age. It supports remote group meetings, audio-video interaction, multi-level group meetings, cross networking, skip-level command, horizontal joint, continuous insertion, autonomous control, plan linkage, on-demand distribution, and flexible reorganization; it must satisfy strategic command smooth migration, tactical end ad hoc access, complex network guaranteed communication, and security </data>
      <data key="d2">doc-0a5b954fbdfaecacdf00721af6b76aff-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Video Warning Control System">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">One of兴图新科's main products; a video warning control system mainly applied to national defense military and extended to prison and oilfield industries.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-0a5b954fbdfaecacdf00721af6b76aff-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Military Command Information System">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">A military command information system of which the military special video command system is an important component.&lt;SEP&gt;The military information system of which the military dedicated video command system is an important component.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-0a5b954fbdfaecacdf00721af6b76aff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Military Special Video Application">
      <data key="d0">concept</data>
      <data key="d1">A military-specific video application characterized by nationwide and grid deployment, network mutual backup, processing multiple signal sources such as video, radar, intelligence, and situation, integrating command, conference, and warning services, and using multiple networks including fiber optic, satellite, industrial 4G, radio, microwave, and DDN dedicated lines.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-0a5b954fbdfaecacdf00721af6b76aff-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General Video Application">
      <data key="d0">concept</data>
      <data key="d1">A general video application characterized by regional deployment, single-system deployment, local standalone backup, processing a single video signal source with one main service such as video conferencing, and using mainly public or local area networks.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-0a5b954fbdfaecacdf00721af6b76aff-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C4ISR System">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">The US military's C4ISR system, to which the C4ISR-Equivalent Engineering Project is equivalent.&lt;SEP&gt;The US military command information system referenced as an equivalent comparison for China's national defense command information system.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. C4ISR system, to which the Certain Intelligence, Command, Control and Communication Network Integration Project is equivalent.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. military's intelligence, command, control, communications, computers, surveillance, and reconnaissance system, to which the Certain Intelligence, Command, Control and Communication Network Integration Projec</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-0a5b954fbdfaecacdf00721af6b76aff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-341185c2a9fbde33b2c43c4a6aef449a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c54e44446e7b57bba54a81c9ed3175f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C4ISR-Equivalent Engineering Project">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">A project equivalent to the US military's C4ISR system, in which兴图新科independently undertook the design, development, and deployment of the video command subsystem, and which overall won the National Science and Technology Progress Award First Prize.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-0a5b954fbdfaecacdf00721af6b76aff-chunk-000</data>
