      <data key="d0">organization</data>
      <data key="d1">The institute that led the Certain Intelligence, Command, Control and Communication Network Integration Project.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Software Layered Design">
      <data key="d0">method</data>
      <data key="d1">The design idea on which the audio-video integrated service platform is based, unifying communication and interface standards and using a loosely coupled model.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Business Component">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">Dozens of independent functional components formed by the audio-video integrated service platform, including device access, signaling dispatch, media forwarding, business management, and permission management components.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Perception Layer">
      <data key="d0">concept</data>
      <data key="d1">A layer that supports the audio-video integrated service platform and includes encoding acquisition, alarm, and positioning modules.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infrastructure Layer">
      <data key="d0">concept</data>
      <data key="d1">A layer that supports the audio-video integrated service platform and includes servers, terminals, storage, and other equipment.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Video Command Application System">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">An application system formed by the audio-video integrated service platform with support from the perception layer and infrastructure layer.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hall Display and Control System">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">An application system formed by the audio-video integrated service platform with support from the perception layer and infrastructure layer.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Video Switching Product">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">A product independently developed by Xingtu Xinke that, in an ideal network environment, enables a single switching device to achieve high-throughput, low-latency video switching with more than 70% bandwidth utilization, and in extreme non-ideal network environments with 100 ms–200 ms propagation delay and 20%–30% packet loss rate, still guarantees low-latency video transmission quality.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Video Codec">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">A codec independently developed by Xingtu Xinke that simultaneously supports the H.265 international standard, the AVS2 national standard, and the JAVS military national standard, and can provide real-time encoding and decoding products supporting all three standards.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="H.265 International Standard">
      <data key="d0">concept</data>
      <data key="d1">The latest international video coding standard supported by Xingtu Xinke's video codec.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AVS2 National Standard">
      <data key="d0">concept</data>
      <data key="d1">The latest national video coding standard supported by Xingtu Xinke's video codec.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JAVS Military National Standard">
      <data key="d0">concept</data>
      <data key="d1">The latest military national video coding standard supported by Xingtu Xinke's video codec.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Domestic FPGA Chip">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">A domestically produced FPGA chip on which Xingtu Xinke's low-latency video encoder is based.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Low-Latency Video Encoder">
      <data key="d0">artifact</data>
      <data key="d1">A low-latency video encoder independently developed by Xingtu Xinke based on a domestic FPGA chip.</data>
      <data key="d2">doc-f65d014acc6991a87f34af637ace18b5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d3">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
